\f1\fs22 Chip hadn\'92t expected visitors. He certainly hadn\'92t expected a TV personality. With a camera operator and sound engineer in tow. The lighting briefly blinded him. He remained sitting on the bunk.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 They always
\f1\i0  
\f2\i looked smaller in real life
\f1\i0 , Chip thought, once his pupils adjusted, more out of melancholy than disappointment. \'93Have you come to execute me for a live studio audience?\'94\
Alexander held up a finger for Chip to wait while he gave it a thought. \'93No, I think Sarah would disapprove.\'94\
\'93Sarah?\'94 Chip\'92s hopes improved.\
\'93Mr Stockwell, I\'92d like to interview you for an episode.\'94\
\'93As long as I\'92m not the star of the show.\'94\
\'93No, no, I\'92m the star. And you are not the focus of the episode.\'94\
\'93Can you get me out of here?\'94\
Alexander nodded absent-mindedly. \'93What? Oh, yes, that could be a good plot point.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'93Good.\'94 Alexander waved the crew in to start recording. \'93I understand you have concerns about Project Kebab.\'94\
Chip\'92s hackles rose. \'93How do you know about that?\'94\
Alexander smiled. \'93I\'92m married to the project director.\'94\
\'93You make it sound like you own the project director.\'94\
Alexander considered that. \'93As much as anyone could own Sarah, I suppose. Her independence just makes me want to make her mine all the more, you know.\'94\
\'93She\'92s good at making people do as she asks,\'94 Chip conceded.\
\'93Yes, well, I\'92m still the head of the house, you understand.\'94\
Chip nodded and grunted. \'93Yes. I have concerns. Concerns I\'92ve expressed. And which landed me here.\'94\
\'93Go on.\'94\
Chip studied Alexander and gave himself half the chances this would make matters worse. He was still wary of the camera but he couldn\'92t have shut himself up, even if he\'92d ever developed the discipline. \'93What happened is that I told your mother something she didn\'92t want to hear.\'94\
\'93Could you repeat that again, but refer to her by name?\'94\
\'93What happened is that I told Eloise Shakti something she didn\'92t want to hear.\'94\
\'93And what was that?\'94\
\'93That Project Kebab was conducting increasingly dangerous experiments,\'94 Chip said. \'93They could rip the fundamental fabric of space-time.\'94\
\'93Like a pair of stockings.\'94\
Chip had judged people to be idiots before, but this perhaps was record time. Still, this one could get him out of there. \'93Yes, if you ripped them with a thermonuclear accident.\'94\
\'93Or a light sabre.\'94\
Chip took a long breath. \'93Sure.\'94\
\'93Who funds Project Kebab?\'94\
\'93Your moth\'97Eloise Shakti.\'94\
\'93Answer that one more time, please.\'94\
\'93Eloise Shakti.\'94\
\'93So, Eloise Shakti could kill us all.\'94\
\'93Her and that dashboard bubble head, Johnny Stoat.\'94\
\'93Please tell us who this Johnny Stoat is.\'94\
\'93He\'92s the one who always manages to find the\'97\'94 Chip almost blundered into naming the discs. \'93He procures the kebabs.\'94\
\'93So he buys you lunch.\'94\
\'93Yes,\'94 Chip answered tersely, wanting to avoid revealing the discs. \'93Eloise Shakti pays him handsomely for it.\'94\
\'93Is Eloise Shakti aware that Project Kebab could rend the stockings of space-time?\'94\
\'93She understands enough to know why I object.\'94\
\'93But she\'92s continuing.\'94\
\'93Yes.\'94\
\'93And you\'92re here.\'94\
Chip spread his hands. There wasn\'92t much room to demonstrate.\
\'93What does Sarah say about it?\'94\
\'93Ms Jacobson took my warnings seriously.\'94\
Alexander was pleased.\
\'93So did Ms Lanning.\'94\
Less pleased.\
\'93Then why haven\'92t they stopped it?\'94\
\'93You\'92d have to ask your mother. You\'92d have to ask Eloise Shakti.\'94\
Whatever else Alexander was inept at, he knew when an interviewee was holding back.\
\'93Is the purpose of Project Kebab to develop new weapons?\'94\
\'93Yes?\'94\
\'93Terrifying weapons?\'94\
\'93Yes.\'94\
\'93Could you state that for the camera please.\'94\
\'93The technology being developed by Project Kebab has applications for weapons.\'94\
\'93Terrifying\'85\'94 Alexander prompted.\
\'93Terrifying new weapons.\'94\
\'93What is the nature of these weapons?\'94\
\'93That\'92s classified.\'94\
\'93By the government.\'94\
\'93Not exactly.\'94\
\'93Then who?\'94\
\'93That\'92s classified.\'94\
Alexander signalled the camera operator to cut, and said to Chip, \'93If you want me to help you, you need to help me.\'94\
Chip grumbled.\
\'93Roll camera,\'94 Alexander instructed. \'93What is the nature of these weapons?\'94\
Chip considered his answer. \'93They can cause targeted\'85 activity, that appears to be a natural disaster.\'94\
Alexander blinked his beady, koala eyes. \'93Like, what? Bushfires? Floods? Black Friday Sale?\'94\
Chip looked into the middle distance and saw only the blurred walls of the cell. \'93On that scale, yes.\'94\
\'93Can you substantiate what you\'92re saying?\'94\
Chip\'92s jaw tightened. \'93There are records.\'94\
\'93Of previous incidents?\'94\
\'93Yes.\'94\
\'93Of\'85\'94\
\'93Targeted, induced natural disasters. I can\'92t say more. The details are classified.\'94\
\'93Then we won\'92t discuss it.\'94\
Chip blinked.\
Fridge Force had not ceased to exist because he was inside somebody else\'92s prison. There were men in that organisation who could turn a badly chosen sentence into several centuries of poor accommodation. He had expected to spend the next few minutes explaining this to a television personality.\
Alexander had already moved on. \'93Are you a spy?\'94\
\'93No.\'94\
Alexander clapped his hands once. \'93Good enough for me.\'94\
Chip looked at the camera again. \'93What?\'94\
\'93I believe you,\'94 Alexander said.\
\'93So you\'92re springing me out of here?\'94\
\'93Yes.\'94\
\'93And I\'92m not the \'91special guest\'92 for any of your episodes.\'94\
\'93No, Mr Stockwell. You are free to go.\'94\
Chip stood, his bulk making Alexander feel like a mid-size marsupial. \'93Thank you.\'94\
\'93Thank Sarah.\'94\
Chip stepped out of the cell. The camera operator backed away to accommodate him. Alexander looked him over: the size, the blunt seriousness, the disinclination to smile. With the right lighting, nobody would doubt this man had warned somebody.\
\'93Put him back.\'94\
Eloise stood at the foot of the stairs. The camera operator started rolling again.\
Alexander turned with his television smile already forming. \'93Mother. Mr Stockwell has been telling me\'97\'94\
\'93I\'92m sure he has. Turn that camera off.\'94\
The operator kept shooting. He was a professional, possibly a dead professional.\
\'93Mother. Your timing is perfect.\'94\
\'93Oh, do please be quiet, Alexander. The adults need to threaten each other.\'94\
Chip and Eloise exchanged terse words with each other, the nature of which we have already narrated, so let\'92s just jump over all that, other than to say that, during the exchange, Alexander had been watching the two security personnel behind his mother who had their rifles trained resolutely on Chip\'92s hulking head. It would be safe to say that neither had heard a word before of Project Kebab or the dangers of the tests, or the shaky goings-on in the Gibson Desert. As Chip loomed like a he-bear over the she-parrot figure that Eloise cut\'97a parrot clasping in her feminine bird-sized claw a handbag that would require anyone on their salary to enter into a mortgage and a kidney exchange contract to possess\'97the guards found themselves siding with Chip\'92s directness over their employer\'92s sharp-witted witchery. \
\'93I have listened, Mr Stockwell. You appear to confuse being heard with being obeyed,\'94 the guards heard Eloise say, and liked none of it.\
Alexander saw it\'97saw the rifle barrels wavering then lowering, so they were no longer aimed at Chip\'92s chest and had drifted to somewhere near his navel.\
\'93Mother,\'94 Alexander said, \'93I think we should all go to the auditorium.\'94\
\'93You have no idea what you\'92re interfering with,\'94 Eloise said.\
The rifles were aimlessly pointing at Chip\'92s knees.\
\'93Boys,\'94 Alexander said to the guards. \'93Take this woman into custody.\'94
